<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<sample title="Object Extern">
	<sdk_desc>Adding custom objects created via API to the world by using <b>ObjectExtern</b>. Implementation of custom rendering, physics, and properties while maintaining full Engine integration.</sdk_desc>
	<desc>
		<brief>
			<para>UNIGINE allows you to extend its out-of-the-box functionality in various ways, including adding your own objects with custom geometry and behavior (e.g., custom particle systems, meshes with custom culling, animated GPU-based crowd rendering solutions, etc.).</para>
			<para>This sample demonstrates how to implement custom user objects based on the <strong nt="1"><link to="objectextern_class">ObjectExtern</link></strong> class, incorporating custom rendering, physics, and properties, while maintaining full Engine integration. These objects can then be added to your scene via API.</para>
		</brief>
	</desc>
	<tags>
		<tag>Objects</tag>
		<tag>Extension &amp; Customization</tag>
	</tags>
</sample>